== not_a_direction
error[Z0402]: `up` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:49
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(direction: up)
  |                                                 ^^ expected one of hv, vh, mid

== a_direction_in_quotes
error[Z0403]: expected one of hv, vh, mid, found text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:49
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(direction: "hv")
  |                                                 ^^^^ a word, not a string
  |
  = help: write the word without quotes: `hv`

== the_plot_maps_no_y
error[Z0401]: `step` places each mark by its `x` and its `y`, but the plot maps no variable to `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:21
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month).step()
  |                     ^^^^ needs both `x` and `y`
  |
  = help: map both where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ, y: wage)`

== a_colour_by_a_number
error[Z0401]: `step` draws each line in one colour, so `color` must show categories, but `percent` is a Float without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:45
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(color: percent)
  |                                             ^^^^^^^ a colour for each row, not for each line
  |
  = help: colour the lines by a variable of categories, as in `step(color: union)`, or set one colour for this layer, as in `step(color: "black")`

== not_a_type
error[Z0401]: `linetype:` of `step` is "stairs", which is not a type of line
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:48
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(linetype: "stairs")
  |                                                ^^^^^^^^ not a type of line
  |
  = help: a type of line is one of solid, dashed, dotted, dash_dot, long_dash and dash_dot_dot

== no_width
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `step` is the width of a line in points of 1/72 inch, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:45
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(width: 0)
  |                                             ^ not a width
  |
  = help: write a width such as 0.5 or 2; without `width:` a line is 1 wide

== no_such_variable
error[Z0101]: no variable `percnt` in `rate`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:41
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(y: percnt)
  |                                         ^^^^^^ not a variable of rate
  |
  = help: did you mean `percent`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"percent"`

== step_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `step` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | rate.step()
  | ^^^^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `step` takes a Plot first; `x.step(...)` is `step(x, ...)`

== no_alpha_on_step
error[Z0404]: `step` has no argument called `alpha`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:38
  |
2 | rate.plot(x: month, y: percent).step(alpha: 0.5)
  |                                      ^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `p.step(data: Frame, x: Var | Expr, y: Var | Expr, color: Var | Str, group: Var, linetype: Var | Str, width: Float = 1, direction: hv | vh | mid = hv)`
